  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The compass – run to the right cone and play first time",
  "description": "Players work in pairs. Each pair sets out a square of four cones, a few metres a side. If you have cones in different colours, use the colours; otherwise name the cones by where they stand as seen from the passer: near left, near right, far left and far right. A stands in the middle of the square and B is outside it with the ball.\n\nB calls a cone. A moves there, receives the pass from B and plays it straight back. Then back to the middle to wait for the next call. Swap roles after about a minute.\n\nVariant: B does not call but points at the cone with the stick, so A has to watch B all the time. Next step: A receives, turns and carries the ball round the cone before passing back. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Move towards the ball as you receive – do not wait for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Play it straight back, flat and onto the passer's stick."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Eyes on the passer while you move, not on the floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Get back to the middle quickly so you are ready for the next cone."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
